01:11:14.360 --> 01:11:18.360
 And so I think with the cemetery, I think I've said it a lot in the past and I think we'll

01:11:18.360 --> 01:11:19.360
 continue to see it.

01:11:19.360 --> 01:11:23.360
 It's an exponential growth thing that we'll grow into.

01:11:23.360 --> 01:11:27.360
 We do have some money for a facilities plan.

01:11:27.360 --> 01:11:32.360
 I don't think that the shed that they're looking at needs to be a large shed to hold equipment in.

01:11:32.360 --> 01:11:34.360
 I don't think that's the need.

01:11:34.360 --> 01:11:41.360
 I think it's just for some of the smaller odds and ends so that we have it on site so we can just pull it and use it when necessary.

01:11:41.360 --> 01:11:45.360
 Instead of trying to gather it up every day and then haul it back to the public works building.

01:11:45.360 --> 01:11:49.360
 So I think that's really what they're after some smaller nature.

01:11:49.360 --> 01:12:00.360
 I think long term we'll have a facility out there that'll probably just be an operational cemetery where that's where somebody goes to to pick the plot and discuss it.

01:12:00.360 --> 01:12:04.360
 And that's I think that's going to how it's going to work long term.

01:12:04.360 --> 01:12:07.360
 We just knew that we'd have to grow into it.

01:12:07.360 --> 01:12:09.360
 We didn't know what it will look like.

01:12:09.360 --> 01:12:16.360
 But I feel like it's like a two year pattern where we like go two years kind of at the same number of areas each year.

01:12:16.360 --> 01:12:19.360
 And then it's like it almost doubles for two years.

01:12:19.360 --> 01:12:22.360
 And then like that's kind of been the trend line.

01:12:22.360 --> 01:12:25.360
 But this year it seems like it's it's it's picked up.

01:12:25.360 --> 01:12:26.360
 We've done quite a few more.

01:12:26.360 --> 01:12:32.360
 I think it's 65,000 people close to 70 where we're probably going to see more.

01:12:32.360 --> 01:12:36.360
 Yeah, because I mean, I think I honestly think we're probably in a three or four year window.

01:12:36.360 --> 01:12:40.360
 We're probably going to have to build the next phase just looking at the numbers.

01:12:40.360 --> 01:12:41.360
 Wait.

01:12:41.360 --> 01:12:42.360
 Can I ask a question?

01:12:42.360 --> 01:12:43.360
 Yeah.

01:12:43.360 --> 01:12:45.360
 Can you because I'm never going to be able to ask this question again.

01:12:45.360 --> 01:12:57.360
 Why would we put a staff member out there dedicated just to cemetery versus having a staff member like at City Hall or something like that for selling plots and talking.

01:12:57.360 --> 01:12:58.360
 So.

01:12:58.360 --> 01:13:00.360
 Or did you not say that because I thought.

01:13:00.360 --> 01:13:03.360
 So I said I think that it will I think it will go to that.

01:13:03.360 --> 01:13:05.360
 I think it'll be busy enough.

01:13:05.360 --> 01:13:11.360
 I mean, just looking at every other municipal cemetery that's in the state in a region.

01:13:11.360 --> 01:13:17.360
 That's what they turn into because it's maintenance and upkeep and people have questions about headstones.

01:13:17.360 --> 01:13:25.360
 And I mean, so if you don't have somebody out there like are they going to go out there and then are we going to make them come to City Hall wherever that City Hall is located.

01:13:25.360 --> 01:13:31.360
 At some point I think it's going to make sense to have an onsite like this is what we have available.

01:13:31.360 --> 01:13:33.360
 This is what you can expect.

01:13:33.360 --> 01:13:35.360
 This is where we store our equipment.

01:13:35.360 --> 01:13:37.360
 So like a sextant or something different.

01:13:37.360 --> 01:13:38.360
 A sextant.

01:13:38.360 --> 01:13:39.360
 There's probably going to be a crew.

01:13:39.360 --> 01:13:42.360
 Most most cemeteries that are larger in size.

01:13:42.360 --> 01:13:44.360
 So like American Fork.

01:13:44.360 --> 01:13:49.360
 They don't have a staff of like 10 but they have a sextant and then they have like two full time.

01:13:49.360 --> 01:13:50.360
 And then they hire some seasonals.

01:13:50.360 --> 01:13:51.360
 On site.

01:13:51.360 --> 01:13:52.360
 What's that?

01:13:52.360 --> 01:13:53.360
 On site.

01:13:53.360 --> 01:13:54.360
 On site.

01:13:54.360 --> 01:13:55.360
 Okay.

01:13:55.360 --> 01:13:59.360
 But I mean you're talking 20,000 plus graves that they have too that they maintain, right?

01:13:59.360 --> 01:14:01.360
 And they're about out of space.

01:14:01.360 --> 01:14:06.360
 So I don't know what the trigger point is to say like hey this is when you build the building.

01:14:06.360 --> 01:14:09.360
 How full is the cemetery now?

01:14:09.360 --> 01:14:10.360
 The first phase.

01:14:10.360 --> 01:14:16.360
 So I would say internment wise we're not like it's not internments that drive the next phase.

01:14:16.360 --> 01:14:17.360
 It's the sales.

01:14:17.360 --> 01:14:18.360
 It's the sales.

01:14:18.360 --> 01:14:19.360
 Yeah.

01:14:19.360 --> 01:14:22.360
 I haven't looked at it in a while.

01:14:22.360 --> 01:14:26.360
 But I mean we've sold a lot.

01:14:26.360 --> 01:14:33.360
 So maybe we just need to make a plan once we get to this percentage of full we need to talk about the next phase of that.

01:14:33.360 --> 01:14:38.360
 We need to build the next phase which I think we've kind of already identified like there's a 17 acre piece.

01:14:38.360 --> 01:14:45.360
 My thought just since we're on the topic is I think that you would build the next phase directly to the west.

01:14:45.360 --> 01:14:50.360
 You would loop the road around it so that we have a connected loop that goes through the cemetery.

01:14:50.360 --> 01:14:52.360
 That makes that seems like that makes the most sense to me.

01:14:52.360 --> 01:14:53.360
 Yeah.

01:14:53.360 --> 01:14:55.360
 And then you continue to phase out from there.

01:14:55.360 --> 01:15:03.360
 But I think we do need to go through the master plan and just understand make sure that we're getting all the components of the cemetery that we need.

01:15:03.360 --> 01:15:04.360
 Thanks.

01:15:04.360 --> 01:15:09.360
 So we've sold approximately a little over 600 spaces.

01:15:09.360 --> 01:15:15.360
 And there's a lot of time dedicated into meeting with people going through that process.

01:15:15.360 --> 01:15:18.360
 And then record keeping is the other component of it.

01:15:18.360 --> 01:15:19.360
 So.

01:15:19.360 --> 01:15:21.360
 But right now that's where our numbers are.

01:15:21.360 --> 01:15:22.360
 Do you know.

01:15:22.360 --> 01:15:27.360
 Do you know how many lots percentage wise we have sold or have left.

01:15:27.360 --> 01:15:34.360
 So we have approximately it's just under 1600 total.

01:15:34.360 --> 01:15:36.360
 And we've sold 600.

01:15:36.360 --> 01:15:37.360
 Okay.

01:15:37.360 --> 01:15:38.360
 Okay.

01:15:38.360 --> 01:15:39.360
 We're not quite halfway there.

01:15:39.360 --> 01:15:40.360
 We're getting about halfway.

01:15:40.360 --> 01:15:48.360
 But I, but I'm just, I'm, I'm projecting off the exponential growth factor that that's going to continue to kind of keep trend.

01:15:48.360 --> 01:15:49.360
 And that's what I'm saying.

01:15:49.360 --> 01:15:52.360
 I think three or four years, I think we're going to be on track.

01:15:52.360 --> 01:15:53.360
 Okay.

01:15:53.360 --> 01:16:03.360
 Are we bringing in enough from our sales of the cemetery plots to help cover the costs of what it costs us to run the cemetery?

01:16:03.360 --> 01:16:08.360
 Or are we, is there any subsidization from just like the general plan?

01:16:12.360 --> 01:16:15.360
 Basically are the fees covering the cost is what I'm asking.

01:16:15.360 --> 01:16:18.360
 I think to this point, I think everything's been covered.

01:16:18.360 --> 01:16:19.360
 Right.

01:16:19.360 --> 01:16:28.360
 Um, and obviously, um, a lot of that is just because, um, we earmark portions of like the park staff time.

01:16:28.360 --> 01:16:36.360
 So I wouldn't say that it's like 100% to say like for cemetery hours, we're billing all that, those hours, right to cemetery.

01:16:36.360 --> 01:16:38.360
 We bill a percentage.

01:16:38.360 --> 01:16:39.360
 Got it.

01:16:39.360 --> 01:16:50.360
 So as we go on, if we want it to be where we're covering those costs relative to employees and everything, we probably will have to shift some of those to make sure that they more adequately represent that.

01:16:50.360 --> 01:16:51.360
 Okay.

01:16:51.360 --> 01:16:52.360
 Thank you.

01:16:52.360 --> 01:17:00.360
 But I'd say for internments, um, for the fees that we charge, um, the only escalated rate that we have is on Saturday.

01:17:00.360 --> 01:17:04.360
 And that's just to cover overtime costs because it's always overtime.

01:17:04.360 --> 01:17:13.360
 Everything else we've, we've split our staff Monday through Friday to try to keep it reasonable, um, and facilitate any, um, interment within the week.

01:17:13.360 --> 01:17:21.360
 Do we have something built into our process that we reevaluate the costs of the plots and what those costs are?

01:17:21.360 --> 01:17:24.360
 Do we do that every five years, 10 years or anything like that?

01:17:24.360 --> 01:17:25.360
 Yeah.

01:17:25.360 --> 01:17:26.360
 We never did build anything into it.

01:17:26.360 --> 01:17:31.360
 Um, I know that when we implemented it, we implemented that at a really low rate.

01:17:31.360 --> 01:17:32.360
 Right.

01:17:32.360 --> 01:17:37.360
 Um, I'd say we're probably one of the cheapest in Utah County by far.

01:17:37.360 --> 01:17:42.360
 Um, and so at some point, yeah, I think it is going to be something that we're going to have to look at.

01:17:42.360 --> 01:17:48.360
 I just, I'm thinking historically like how the water rates didn't get changed or adjusted for 20 years.

01:17:48.360 --> 01:17:51.360
 And then all of a sudden it's just this big change.

01:17:51.360 --> 01:18:01.360
 And, um, I, I would like for us to build in check marks along the way so that we can say, is it time to make a change?

01:18:01.360 --> 01:18:05.360
 Oh, no, not, you know, like, and just at least look at it.

01:18:05.360 --> 01:18:12.360
 Otherwise we're caught down the road and we're subsidizing half of the cost of it because we didn't evaluate prices.

01:18:12.360 --> 01:18:23.360
 So, and I think some cities that are really escalated in their grave site purchases are ones that are running out of space, right?

01:18:23.360 --> 01:18:26.360
 The more, like the less space you have, the more expensive they get.

01:18:26.360 --> 01:18:31.360
 Um, and you know, with us, I think it's something that we can definitely look at.

01:18:31.360 --> 01:18:38.360
 Um, another factor that could come into play is I know Saratoga Springs is looking to build a cemetery as well right now.

01:18:38.360 --> 01:18:44.360
 And so I don't know what that impact is going to be to us because I think we've, um, we've been, uh,

01:18:44.360 --> 01:18:50.360
 our cemetery has been a place where Saratoga residents have been buried in our cemetery as well.

01:18:50.360 --> 01:18:53.360
 So we've got some factors.

01:18:53.360 --> 01:18:54.360
 Thank you.

01:18:54.360 --> 01:18:58.360
 This might apply to you too, but I have, uh, two questions.

01:18:58.360 --> 01:19:01.360
 One, uh, I'll start with the easy one.

01:19:01.360 --> 01:19:04.360
 I talked to Zach last night about that Kubota tractor.

01:19:04.360 --> 01:19:07.360
 I know almost every department has used that.

01:19:07.360 --> 01:19:10.360
 And the last time I saw it, it was pretty rough shape.

01:19:10.360 --> 01:19:14.360
 Is the parks department, I don't think the streets department uses it hardly at all anymore.

01:19:14.360 --> 01:19:16.360
 Is the parks department using that?

01:19:16.360 --> 01:19:18.360
 And what's the condition that's in there?

01:19:18.360 --> 01:19:24.360
 Or what other departments are using that's what I'm curious on.

01:19:24.360 --> 01:19:25.360
 We use it.

01:19:25.360 --> 01:19:30.360
 Um, and when we use it, we, I mean, I would say most of the time it's for like brush hogging.

01:19:30.360 --> 01:19:32.360
 Cutting weeds.

01:19:32.360 --> 01:19:33.360
 Is it still attachments?

01:19:33.360 --> 01:19:36.360
 Sufficiently operational?

01:19:36.360 --> 01:19:37.360
 It seems like.

01:19:37.360 --> 01:19:39.360
 I mean, I think it's been working, right?

01:19:39.360 --> 01:19:40.360
 No.

01:19:40.360 --> 01:19:47.360
 So do you have a, and maybe Jeff knows too, but is there a, a timeline on replacement for that?

01:19:47.360 --> 01:19:50.360
 No, me and you had this discussion kind of on the side.

01:19:50.360 --> 01:19:54.360
 And I, I, I think we need to look at that on that piece of equipment.

01:19:54.360 --> 01:20:00.360
 I don't think it's ever been built in to say, hey, here's a depreciation rate on this and we're going to replace it on X day.

01:20:00.360 --> 01:20:02.360
 So it's probably something that we need to look at.

01:20:02.360 --> 01:20:06.360
 That's, that's why I was wondering because it's still, you know, I mean, it's not on here.

01:20:06.360 --> 01:20:12.360
 And I think it's probably something that's been pretty vital to the city and in almost every department at some time.

01:20:12.360 --> 01:20:15.360
 But, and I don't know if anyone else has anything on that one.

01:20:15.360 --> 01:20:17.360
 But my other question is the fifth wheel trailer.

01:20:17.360 --> 01:20:19.360
 Is that a flatbed gooseneck?

01:20:19.360 --> 01:20:21.360
 Is that what we're looking at here?

01:20:21.360 --> 01:20:27.360
 Flatbed or a camp trailer or that's for you?

01:20:27.360 --> 01:20:28.360
 Yes, sir.

01:20:28.360 --> 01:20:29.360
 Flatbed?

01:20:29.360 --> 01:20:30.360
 Flatbed.

01:20:30.360 --> 01:20:35.360
 I'm going to ask a question to Brad about coming back to the tractor.

01:20:35.360 --> 01:20:44.360
 Well, we know that there's a number of these places that we keep talking about that need to be brought up to a better standard that belong to us.

01:20:44.360 --> 01:20:48.360
 Is one tractor with the bush hog on it going to be enough to take care of those?

01:20:48.360 --> 01:20:51.360
 Or are we waiting?

01:20:51.360 --> 01:20:57.360
 So I think in the next couple of years, I think we'll have some options that we'll bring forward.

01:20:57.360 --> 01:21:03.360
 I can see some of our open space maintenance changing and evolving for years.

01:21:03.360 --> 01:21:07.360
 Like we've just covered it underneath the contract and we're going to continue to have open space.

01:21:07.360 --> 01:21:16.360
 The difference being when we start establishing some of these open space areas and we define what they are, the maintenance standards might change.

01:21:16.360 --> 01:21:19.360
 Like so some years we might not even cut.

01:21:19.360 --> 01:21:24.360
 And it might be more of like a chemical treatment to cut down on the noxious weeds or whatever it is, right?

01:21:24.360 --> 01:21:27.360
 And so that maintenance level will be different.

01:21:27.360 --> 01:21:34.360
 And so I think we've just got to, as a department, we've got to, and as a city, we've got to work together to try to define like, what is that standard?

01:21:34.360 --> 01:21:36.360
 What is it we want it to look like?

01:21:36.360 --> 01:21:47.360
 And then once we can establish that and then we can quantify like acreage wise, what we're doing, then we can say, okay, actually, if we are going to cut this amount every year, it's probably would be good to maybe have two tractors.

01:21:47.360 --> 01:21:50.360
 I just can't quantify it at this point because I don't know.

01:21:50.360 --> 01:21:51.360
 That's what I was asking.

01:21:51.360 --> 01:21:52.360
 Thanks.

01:21:52.360 --> 01:21:53.360
 All right.

01:21:53.360 --> 01:21:59.360
 Mayor, in council, just because I know that we're pushing it up for us to jump into that policy session and stuff.

01:21:59.360 --> 01:22:08.360
 I'd like to take just a few more minutes because I know what's on the policy session and I think we'll be able to get that done really quick.

01:22:08.360 --> 01:22:09.360
 Right?

01:22:09.360 --> 01:22:12.360
 Between, so you'll get this list.

01:22:12.360 --> 01:22:14.360
 This list is going to go out to you.

01:22:14.360 --> 01:22:19.360
 You'll get the list of the capital projects so you'll be able to see what they are.

01:22:19.360 --> 01:22:33.360
 You know, within the next week, if you are seeing anything that you guys have concerns about or want to be able to have some discussion further on those items that you'd like us to make a change before things come forward in the tentative budget, then please reach out.

01:22:33.360 --> 01:22:47.360
 But while you're collectively here as a body, I do want to take a few minutes to just talk about some three items that we have that are on our list that stem around our communications and kind of continued branding that we have for the city.

01:22:47.360 --> 01:23:00.360
 So, and I know that Tyler has some additional information and that he's here to be able to address any questions that you might have related to that.

01:23:00.360 --> 01:23:15.360
 So, again, for the branding update, the monument signs, the new wayfinding signs, public art installation stuff, that particular component of it is looking at just under $300,000.

01:23:15.360 --> 01:23:24.360
 And then we have branding spaces in terms of the council chambers, office spaces, cubicle plaques, those types of things at $12,000.

01:23:24.360 --> 01:23:28.360
 And then a marketing initiative that's around $18,000.

01:23:28.360 --> 01:23:38.360
 So, I would like to be able to allow you to ask any questions you specifically have to Tyler regarding those as we continue to move these forward.

01:23:39.360 --> 01:23:41.360
 Can I ask a question?

01:23:41.360 --> 01:23:45.360
 I want to know if this is all new money, right?

01:23:45.360 --> 01:23:49.360
 On top of what we spent in the branding thing to this point.

01:23:49.360 --> 01:23:56.360
 Which at this point, every time we have a change order or whatever in branding, I keep saying, I knew this was going to cost a lot of money.

01:23:56.360 --> 01:23:58.360
 Can you give me an idea of what we spent so far?

01:23:58.360 --> 01:24:01.360
 I'm guessing between $300,000 and $500,000.

01:24:02.360 --> 01:24:03.360
 More?

01:24:03.360 --> 01:24:10.360
 So, I can't give you a specific number right now, but between the website, which is branding related,

01:24:10.360 --> 01:24:19.360
 changing over some of our logos for projects that were allocated for in phase one in fiscal year 2024,

01:24:19.360 --> 01:24:24.360
 in the fiscal year 2024 budget, and the actual process of changing over our--

01:24:24.360 --> 01:24:26.360
 The consultant, the design, all the--

01:24:26.360 --> 01:24:27.360
 Mm-hmm.

01:24:27.360 --> 01:24:31.360
 I would put it at around $300,000 right now.

01:24:31.360 --> 01:24:35.360
 So, we're looking at six, you know.

01:24:35.360 --> 01:24:37.360
 I said we'd be over a million dollars before we were done.

01:24:37.360 --> 01:24:39.360
 And I think I'm going to be close.

01:24:39.360 --> 01:24:48.360
 Well, I think it's important to keep in mind, much of this would have been contemplating either way.

01:24:48.360 --> 01:24:56.360
 I mean, because there's stuff that's, like, some of the wayfinding we've just been holding up on and some of the other stuff.

01:24:56.360 --> 01:25:05.360
 You know, I guess we decide just to keep all the old eclectic signage or, you know.

01:25:05.360 --> 01:25:10.360
 I'm going to laugh because I'm going to say it was a 4-1 vote every single time.

01:25:10.360 --> 01:25:12.360
 It probably means I just needed to get on board with it.

01:25:12.360 --> 01:25:16.360
 But every single time was because of the money, and I just--

01:25:16.360 --> 01:25:19.360
 And you're right, I think a lot of this is probably needed anyway.

01:25:19.360 --> 01:25:21.360
 So, might as well have a new sticker instead of an old one.

01:25:21.360 --> 01:25:25.360
 So, maybe some of that plays into it, it just wasn't--

01:25:25.360 --> 01:25:28.360
 Can I ask what the public art project is?

01:25:28.360 --> 01:25:30.360
 Yeah, yeah, I'm glad you asked about that.

01:25:30.360 --> 01:25:34.360
 So, part of the phasing, and I just want to know for the record that it does not--

01:25:34.360 --> 01:25:37.360
 that does not have to be done this coming fiscal year.

01:25:37.360 --> 01:25:47.360
 But a major goal of the branding committee and of this rebranding effort is overall to improve and elevate the look and feel of the community.

01:25:47.360 --> 01:25:56.360
 And so, among some pretty lengthy discussions with the branding committee, we considered one of the silos that we're focusing on,

01:25:56.360 --> 01:26:00.360
 which is resident quality of life, that public art would be a major component of that.

01:26:00.360 --> 01:26:09.360
 We're very cautious, and we're very considerate, and we're very aware that we need to see this through the lens that that has been unsuccessful in the past.

01:26:09.360 --> 01:26:18.360
 But we do feel that making a first move and a first step toward that, that the council adopted a public art code last year,

01:26:18.360 --> 01:26:28.360
 that this would be a good time to make a tiny step forward on that as part of overall efforts to elevate that look and feel as part of rebranding.

01:26:28.360 --> 01:26:29.360
 Can I ask a question?

01:26:29.360 --> 01:26:30.360
 Do we know what it is?

01:26:30.360 --> 01:26:31.360
 We don't.

01:26:31.360 --> 01:26:41.360
 So, we have a preliminary staff report to get us started, and then we're hoping that that will lead into more comprehensive efforts that we would bring back and talk with the council about.

01:26:41.360 --> 01:26:45.360
 How much of that budget is contemplated towards the public art?

01:26:45.360 --> 01:26:47.360
 One hundred thousand dollars just this year.

01:26:47.360 --> 01:26:48.360
 Okay.

01:26:48.360 --> 01:26:49.360
 Thank you.

01:26:49.360 --> 01:26:50.360
 Councilmember Clark?

01:26:50.360 --> 01:27:06.360
 Well, I'm just wondering, like when you guys passed the branding, did you have the idea that that would involve public art and updating office and cubicle plaques and conference rooms and like all of those other things?

01:27:06.360 --> 01:27:11.360
 Like, because I guess the question is, where does it stop?

01:27:11.360 --> 01:27:12.360
 We could rebrand everything.

01:27:12.360 --> 01:27:23.360
 We could paint this room orange if we wanted to, but at what point is what you guys approved when you approved it, what was contemplated and planned?

01:27:23.360 --> 01:27:27.360
 Because there's more and more things that keep getting added to it.

01:27:27.360 --> 01:27:33.360
 And I think we need to be mindful of that because, yeah, it would be nice to improve the way of life for our residents.

01:27:33.360 --> 01:27:35.360
 But you know what's really nice?

01:27:35.360 --> 01:27:38.360
 Them having enough money to be able to buy groceries and put gas in their car.

01:27:38.360 --> 01:27:48.360
 So I just thinking like we need to have a better idea of where we're headed with this instead of bringing back stuff.

01:27:48.360 --> 01:27:55.360
 Because you mentioned even when you talked about the public art item, you said that's a hundred thousand dollars for this year only.

01:27:55.360 --> 01:28:00.360
 So does that mean that there's a plan to spend 200 next year and the year after that?

01:28:00.360 --> 01:28:02.360
 Like, is that part of the plan?

01:28:02.360 --> 01:28:07.360
 The council has an appetite for comprehensive plans to be completed.

01:28:07.360 --> 01:28:13.360
 I think the branding committee is more than prepared to bring those forward so that there's a better picture for what the end game is.

01:28:13.360 --> 01:28:21.360
 What I don't want to put forward and what I don't want to instill here is that this is nebulously moving forward with a never-ending cost and spiral.

01:28:21.360 --> 01:28:23.360
 I don't think that's the goal.

01:28:23.360 --> 01:28:29.360
 I think this is a good way to set the table for the generalized goal of elevating the look and feel of the community.

01:28:29.360 --> 01:28:36.360
 I understand that there are necessary concerns for being very fiscally prudent with taxpayer dollars.

01:28:36.360 --> 01:28:43.360
 And at the same time, I think there are some really key things that ought to be focused on at the same time to complete it and complete it well.

01:28:43.360 --> 01:28:46.360
 Or at the same time, balancing that against our fiscal constraints.

01:28:46.360 --> 01:28:49.360
 I would say that if you have a plan, we'd like to see it.

01:28:49.360 --> 01:28:50.360
 Yeah, absolutely.

01:28:50.360 --> 01:28:54.360
 Because that at least gives us an idea of what the overall spend is going to be for it.

01:28:54.360 --> 01:29:02.360
 It gives the council the opportunity to say, yes, we're on board with it or maybe not all of it, maybe these things or not at all.

01:29:02.360 --> 01:29:05.360
 And I think that's important to be able to make that decision.

01:29:05.360 --> 01:29:08.360
 So we're not, I agree with council member Clark.

01:29:08.360 --> 01:29:13.360
 There needs to be an idea of what the end goal of this is and what the overall cost is.

01:29:13.360 --> 01:29:20.360
 Because the reality is, is we're taking this money from other places that we want to make sure we're comfortable with doing that.

01:29:20.360 --> 01:29:21.360
 Understood.

01:29:21.360 --> 01:29:23.360
 And I will look toward that.

01:29:23.360 --> 01:29:29.360
 Do you, was the plan not presented to the council when they approved rebranding?

01:29:29.360 --> 01:29:35.360
 It, it very much was as a phase one priority last fiscal year.

01:29:35.360 --> 01:29:43.360
 And then we tapped onto that, the, the website components of it, which was a, a directive given, given to me.

01:29:43.360 --> 01:29:47.360
 And so this, this next fiscal year will be phase two.

01:29:47.360 --> 01:29:49.360
 And so I've got phase two laid out.

01:29:49.360 --> 01:29:55.360
 But if the council is desiring the total picture and ending, then I can get that to you here in the next couple of weeks.

01:29:55.360 --> 01:30:01.360
 And, and we did talk when we had the discussions about phases, more phases to come.

01:30:01.360 --> 01:30:02.360
 So that's.

01:30:02.360 --> 01:30:09.360
 When you guys did that, did you know how many phases there were going to be and about how much it was going to cost and what things were included?

01:30:09.360 --> 01:30:14.360
 Or was it, we're approving phase one, there's going to be more phases, but we're not sure what's in them.

01:30:14.360 --> 01:30:18.360
 I just want to have a better idea of the context of that decision.

01:30:18.360 --> 01:30:22.360
 Can I just have one, a thought here too, that may be helpful.

01:30:22.360 --> 01:30:26.360
 Can I get an answer to the question that I just asked before we move on to that thought?

01:30:26.360 --> 01:30:28.360
 Well, that's what I'm attempting to do.

01:30:28.360 --> 01:30:29.360
 Okay.

01:30:29.360 --> 01:30:31.360
 I'm attempting to give it some context.

01:30:31.360 --> 01:30:41.360
 And then, and then we can go from there, but we're calling this branding, but really this goes back to the visioning.

01:30:41.360 --> 01:30:53.360
 And it's, it's efforts to fulfill, you know, to do the discovery in fulfilling, you know, those, those visioning goals.

01:30:53.360 --> 01:31:08.360
 So with that, I, I don't know if somebody wants to answer that council member Clark's question in more detail, but I, I, I, I'll take a shot at it.

01:31:08.360 --> 01:31:09.360
 Yeah.

01:31:09.360 --> 01:31:10.360
 A little bit.

01:31:10.360 --> 01:31:15.360
 I mean, I, I was here and I, I felt like there was a pretty good sense of where we were headed.

01:31:15.360 --> 01:31:17.360
 At least I, I felt like that.

01:31:17.360 --> 01:31:21.360
 I felt like we understood the basic cost was about that $300,000 mark.

01:31:21.360 --> 01:31:25.360
 We talked about billboards and other things and we removed those from the plan.

01:31:25.360 --> 01:31:26.360
 If you'll remember.

01:31:26.360 --> 01:31:34.360
 Um, I also know that, uh, at least my expectation was, is that there was going to be some additional costs that would come forward as we looked at street signs.

01:31:34.360 --> 01:31:39.360
 Um, the monument signs are kind of new, but certainly an addition or some corrections or changes.

01:31:39.360 --> 01:31:48.360
 I anticipated that there would be some changes that we need to come forward, um, to implement this fully for the city and to, to capture the vision.

01:31:48.360 --> 01:31:52.360
 And, and I might be, maybe I'm the, maybe I'm the only one left.

01:31:52.360 --> 01:31:53.360
 I don't know.

01:31:53.360 --> 01:31:56.360
 Um, we had a hard time with council member Curtis.

01:31:56.360 --> 01:32:02.360
 He was pretty, um, I mean, I love council member Curtis and love serving with him, but he was a little more resistant to this.

01:32:02.360 --> 01:32:05.360
 And, and council member gray has expressed his concerns.

01:32:05.360 --> 01:32:15.360
 And fiscally, it's always, it's always scary when you set money aside to spend it on things like this, because it's not something that you buy and sell.

01:32:15.360 --> 01:32:17.360
 And so you don't see that return on that investment.

01:32:17.360 --> 01:32:22.360
 You don't see that, uh, you know, that it's a tractor that you put out in the cemetery and you dig holes and you use it up.

01:32:23.360 --> 01:32:32.360
 But I personally think from what I've seen, this does elevate Eagle Mountain to a new status and to a new level among, among cities.

01:32:32.360 --> 01:32:34.360
 And, and frankly, I'm interested in that.

01:32:34.360 --> 01:32:43.360
 I think it's important for us to make that statement to say, look, we've moved beyond the country bumpkin hicks that council member writes, which we all were.

01:32:43.360 --> 01:32:53.360
 And, and we've, we've become a little more sophisticated and we're, we're, we're community and team members that matter within the state.

01:32:53.360 --> 01:32:58.360
 And I just feel like this helps to project that and to make that statement.

01:32:58.360 --> 01:33:00.360
 Does it cost us something to accomplish that?

01:33:00.360 --> 01:33:01.360
 Yes.

01:33:01.360 --> 01:33:04.360
 At some point it's going to be too much.

01:33:04.360 --> 01:33:07.360
 We're going to have to say no to X, Y, or Z.

01:33:07.360 --> 01:33:10.360
 What, what kind of image do you want to create for Eagle mountain?

01:33:10.360 --> 01:33:11.360
 That's really the question.

01:33:11.360 --> 01:33:16.360
 And so, and I think that our branding committee has done a beautiful job of doing that.

01:33:16.360 --> 01:33:18.360
 Um, I'm super happy with it.

01:33:18.360 --> 01:33:20.360
 And I may be alone in that.

01:33:20.360 --> 01:33:30.360
 And, and, and I think it's worth some con at least some continuing investment to just follow through with the vision and to give it a chance to plan.

01:33:30.360 --> 01:33:32.360
 Those seeds and let them grow.

01:33:32.360 --> 01:33:34.360
 That's, that's kind of where I'm at with it.

01:33:34.360 --> 01:33:38.360
 And I recognize that we have new council members and we're going to have some new thoughts about that.

01:33:38.360 --> 01:33:42.360
 And, and perhaps some broader discussion that needs to take place.

01:33:42.360 --> 01:33:48.360
 Would you, would you be okay with Tyler bringing forward kind of what the plan that they have?

01:33:48.360 --> 01:33:49.360
 Absolutely.

01:33:49.360 --> 01:33:51.360
 I think that makes a lot of sense.

01:33:51.360 --> 01:33:52.360
 Council member.

01:33:52.360 --> 01:33:54.360
 I don't want you to feel like I'm saying no.

01:33:54.360 --> 01:33:57.360
 I'm just saying, what are we, what are we looking at?

01:33:57.360 --> 01:33:58.360
 What does the future hold?

01:33:58.360 --> 01:33:59.360
 I'll be honest with you.

01:33:59.360 --> 01:34:03.360
 I like the fact that we're going to start doing art in the city.

01:34:03.360 --> 01:34:10.360
 I think those are some of the things that you see in cities all over the state when they start to put forth things that people can go and enjoy.

01:34:10.360 --> 01:34:15.360
 Things that to council member Wright's point, they, they elevate us as a city.

01:34:15.360 --> 01:34:17.360
 They show some sophistication.

01:34:17.360 --> 01:34:20.360
 I'd like them to follow who we are.

01:34:20.360 --> 01:34:21.360
 I want to put that in there.

01:34:21.360 --> 01:34:33.360
 I don't know that we're looking to come up with art that would probably not fit in the community that we are, that would probably be more beneficial in a city that's in an urban environment.

01:34:33.360 --> 01:34:34.360
 Yeah.

01:34:34.360 --> 01:34:36.360
 In fact, Tyler and I spoke about that specifically.

01:34:36.360 --> 01:34:40.360
 What we did not want is a mural in a ghetto, right?

01:34:40.360 --> 01:34:42.360
 That's not what we're talking about here.

01:34:42.360 --> 01:34:43.360
 Yeah.

01:34:43.360 --> 01:34:45.360
 This is, that's not the goal.

01:34:45.360 --> 01:34:46.360
 So.

01:34:46.360 --> 01:34:54.360
 To be fair too, because for me all along, where I struggle, and I was talking to somebody from the Great Depression today, right?

01:34:54.360 --> 01:35:00.360
 That mentality of we reuse and use until it's no longer usable.

01:35:00.360 --> 01:35:06.360
 Where I struggle in the rebranding thing is taking a sticker off a truck just to put another one on that wasn't wore out.

01:35:06.360 --> 01:35:09.360
 Now putting it on a new truck, we would have put the old sticker, new sticker, didn't matter, right?

01:35:09.360 --> 01:35:18.360
 Now having said that, for me the money to just replace something that wasn't broke, but the art project, the 100 grand, we didn't have art.

01:35:18.360 --> 01:35:23.360
 This is something that's part of rebranding, but it's more of we want to beautify.

01:35:23.360 --> 01:35:32.360
 So to be fair, my own, you know, this is allocating money for a project that you can tie it to rebranding, but it's actually above and beyond.

01:35:32.360 --> 01:35:37.360
 It's something that we're not just tearing something down to rebuild it, we're beautifying and adding to.

01:35:37.360 --> 01:35:39.360
 It's creating community identity.

01:35:39.360 --> 01:35:40.360
 Right.

01:35:40.360 --> 01:35:45.360
 I think for me that's the major component to it, is that it creates community identity.

01:35:45.360 --> 01:35:46.360
 Which I'm good with, right?

01:35:46.360 --> 01:35:47.360
 Look, look at my shirt.

01:35:47.360 --> 01:35:48.360
 Yeah, yeah.

01:35:48.360 --> 01:35:49.360
 See?

01:35:49.360 --> 01:35:50.360
 I like it.

01:35:50.360 --> 01:35:51.360
 Yeah, here we are.

01:35:51.360 --> 01:35:52.360
 Me and you.

01:35:52.360 --> 01:35:53.360
 Which do you like better?

01:35:53.360 --> 01:36:02.360
 And I don't mean that facetiously, you know, and I, I mean, I believe in it.

01:36:02.360 --> 01:36:03.360
 I purchased these myself.

01:36:03.360 --> 01:36:05.360
 The city didn't pay for these.

01:36:05.360 --> 01:36:07.360
 These are my shirts and my logos.

01:36:07.360 --> 01:36:12.360
 I paid, no, not my logo, but I paid for the logos to be placed on this shirt.

01:36:12.360 --> 01:36:16.360
 And I just believe in it enough, I think it binds us together.

01:36:16.360 --> 01:36:20.360
 And I, and I'm seeing that in the community.

01:36:20.360 --> 01:36:22.360
 It's just starting to take hold.

01:36:22.360 --> 01:36:25.360
 I'm excited about that because we are different.

01:36:25.360 --> 01:36:27.360
 We do think of ourselves differently.

01:36:27.360 --> 01:36:32.360
 And, and people that come here, they sense and feel that.

01:36:32.360 --> 01:36:34.360
 And they're not sure what it is.

01:36:34.360 --> 01:36:40.360
 But I think this helps to, at least for me, it helps to coalesce that this is what it is.

01:36:40.360 --> 01:36:41.360
 This is what makes it.

01:36:41.360 --> 01:36:42.360
 Can I ask one more question?

01:36:42.360 --> 01:36:43.360
 And I appreciate that.

01:36:43.360 --> 01:36:45.360
 And like I said, I'm kind of getting on board with it anyway.

01:36:45.360 --> 01:36:50.360
 But one of my favorite arguments to have with my little brother, and he likes to have with

01:36:50.360 --> 01:36:55.360
 me more than anything, is once we allocate the money, we don't have no say, meaning the

01:36:55.360 --> 01:36:56.360
 council.

01:36:56.360 --> 01:36:58.360
 He's a city worker in a different city.

01:36:58.360 --> 01:37:05.360
 And so when we approve this funding for say $100,000 worth of art, and then I know Councilman

01:37:05.360 --> 01:37:10.360
 Curtis was really particular about this, is what's the mechanism to make sure that we're

01:37:10.360 --> 01:37:14.360
 not going to get, I don't even want to say woke or whatever, you know, some kind of art

01:37:14.360 --> 01:37:17.360
 project that the council wouldn't be on board with, right?

01:37:17.360 --> 01:37:22.360
 Because literally once we say here's some money, that's where our jurisdiction kind of stops.

01:37:22.360 --> 01:37:23.360
 At least that's what he'd argue.

01:37:23.360 --> 01:37:27.360
 I would say that we probably want to have some say in that one.

01:37:27.360 --> 01:37:30.360
 I would love nothing more than the council have some say in that.

01:37:30.360 --> 01:37:31.360
 Agreed.

01:37:31.360 --> 01:37:32.360
 I would love to understand that once we allocate the money.

01:37:32.360 --> 01:37:38.360
 But look, the procurement code requires that, where this is a visioning or a statement that's

01:37:38.360 --> 01:37:42.360
 associated with council visioning and city identity.

01:37:42.360 --> 01:37:45.360
 The procurement code's going to require that those come back and they're presented to council

01:37:45.360 --> 01:37:46.360
 for approval.

01:37:46.360 --> 01:37:50.360
 So even if that money is set aside in the budget, they're not going to run out and just pick

01:37:50.360 --> 01:37:52.360
 a project and say we're done.

01:37:52.360 --> 01:37:54.360
 That will come to us for approval.

01:37:54.360 --> 01:37:57.360
 We'll have to then sign off on it before it's ever funded.

01:37:57.360 --> 01:37:58.360
 Okay.

01:37:58.360 --> 01:38:00.360
 We're going to have to stop talking.

