 I'll switch places on you. Would it be okay if I presented both of these together?

01:41:03.740 --> 01:41:09.260
 Yeah, okay. Three and four? Yeah, three and four. I did that with the planning commission.

01:41:09.260 --> 01:41:13.400
 Okay, and they're both public hearings, so I think that's fine. Let me go to read four as well.

01:41:13.400 --> 01:41:22.760
 Okay. A resolution of Eagle Mountain City, Utah, amending Eagle Mountain City consolidated fee schedule for building permit fees. Okay, it's yours.

01:41:22.900 --> 01:41:35.660
 Okay, very good. When I presented this to the planning commission earlier today, it flowed better when I kind of treated them together or addressed them together.

01:41:36.020 --> 01:41:42.240
 The planning commission, I will say, heard this earlier today and recommended approval of both of these.

01:41:42.920 --> 01:41:47.980
 What kind of the impetus for this is, well, there's a couple of things.

01:41:48.080 --> 01:42:03.260
 Number one, this idea of trying to clarify some of our, how we treat international codes in our, in chapters 15, title 15, rather.

01:42:03.800 --> 01:42:05.800
 We've been working on that for a little bit.

01:42:06.360 --> 01:42:16.500
 We've also been working to get an electronic permitting system for building permits and, or other types of permits that we do, yeah, community development.

01:42:16.500 --> 01:42:23.180
 And we're going to go live on Monday for, for our planning permits, so that's, we're, we're there.

01:42:23.600 --> 01:42:29.400
 But building ran into a little snag with, with our building fees.

01:42:29.400 --> 01:42:39.660
 And so part of what we're coming here, what we're proposing here will help kind of make that a little, that process a little easier.

01:42:39.660 --> 01:42:54.540
 So we've been working with a company called OpenGov and they have a, a system that's really helpful in, in managing our city permits and the fees, the fees side of that.

01:42:54.540 --> 01:43:00.900
 It's been a little complex the way we, we're currently structured and so forth, it's making a little bit, a little challenging.

01:43:00.900 --> 01:43:04.260
 So this will help, help in that regard.

01:43:04.560 --> 01:43:12.600
 So what this proposal does is, and you've had a, you know, you have a copy of that proposal before you.

01:43:12.600 --> 01:43:18.760
 I'm just going to hit on some important main points in the code here.

01:43:20.300 --> 01:43:30.740
 So one of the things that we've been trying to do is get to the point where we don't have to amend our code every time the city,

01:43:31.140 --> 01:43:35.760
 every time the state legislative session, uh, happens.

01:43:36.080 --> 01:43:45.900
 So, um, we're trying to, if you look in 1595, the first of 15, of our, our city code 1595,

01:43:45.900 --> 01:43:50.140
 you can see that we've got a laundry list of international codes that we've adopted.

01:43:50.820 --> 01:43:57.380
 Um, we can really do that a lot more simply by just adopting the state construction fire code.

01:43:57.380 --> 01:44:03.680
 Because all of those codes are adopted, uh, by the state and we have to comply with them anyway.

01:44:03.680 --> 01:44:14.240
 So, um, so we are proposing here to, to just adopt the state construction fire code and kind of free up a little space in our code there.

01:44:14.240 --> 01:44:21.780
 Um, planning on, uh, another big component of this is referencing current codes.

01:44:21.780 --> 01:44:33.720
 When we're, when we're, when we're citing codes, tables, and so forth, we're saying we're going to, we adopt the current state codes.

01:44:33.720 --> 01:44:43.520
 We adopt the current, um, um, fee, we'll reference the current fees in the consolidated fee schedule.

01:44:43.520 --> 01:45:06.720
 We, uh, we, uh, we, we use the current building valuation table, um, so the, the idea is that if, if we, if we, right now we've, we've, we've got a, we've got a setup so that we, we, we've, we're referencing specific sections of code and then, like I said, we have to come back in amended.

01:45:06.720 --> 01:45:22.560
 But, um, that, so a couple of things, the consolidated fee schedule, we want, as you can see, it's, it's in our code, in our code right now in 1595 and we've also got it in our, um, fee schedule.

01:45:22.560 --> 01:45:27.360
 So, we see no need to have it in, in both the code and the fee schedule.

